msgstr "Botones"

#: includes/admin-social.php:47
msgid "Global settings"
msgstr "Ajustes generales"

#: includes/admin-social.php:80
msgid "Buttons saved."
msgstr "Botones guardados."

#: includes/admin-social.php:97
msgid ""
"One app per network: create it in the provider’s developer console, paste "
"the client ID and the secret, and copy the redirect URL that each card "
"shows. Then run the live test — a provider cannot be enabled until the round"
" trip actually works."
msgstr ""
"Una aplicación por red: se crea en la consola de desarrolladores del "
"proveedor, se pegan aquí el ID de cliente y el secreto, y se copia la URL de"
" retorno que muestra cada tarjeta. Después va la prueba en vivo — una red no"
" se puede activar hasta que el ida y vuelta funcione de verdad."

#: includes/admin-social.php:134 includes/admin-social.php:628
msgid "Disable"
msgstr "Desactivar"

#: includes/admin-social.php:134 includes/admin-social.php:628
msgid "Enable"
msgstr "Activar"

#: includes/admin-social.php:139
msgid "Get started"
msgstr "Cómo empezar"

#: includes/admin-social.php:147
msgid "Not included, on purpose"
msgstr "Lo que no está, a propósito"

#: includes/admin-social.php:149
msgid ""
"Apple signs its client secret with a JWT that has to be regenerated every "
"six months and answers by POST; Steam does not use OAuth 2 at all and never "
"returns an email address. Both need their own flow, so they are not here "
"yet: a button that does not work is worse than no button."
msgstr ""
"Apple firma su secreto de cliente con un JWT que hay que regenerar cada seis"
" meses y responde por POST; Steam directamente no usa OAuth 2 y nunca "
"devuelve el correo. Los dos necesitan su propio flujo, así que todavía no "
"están: un botón que no anda es peor que no tener el botón."

#: includes/admin-social.php:158
msgid "Not set up"
msgstr "Sin configurar"

#: includes/admin-social.php:159
msgid "Needs testing"
msgstr "Falta probarla"

#: includes/admin-social.php:160
msgid "Disabled"
msgstr "Desactivada"

#: includes/admin-social.php:179
msgid ""
"How the buttons look on the sign-in page. It is the same markup and the same"
" stylesheet the site uses, so the preview is the real thing."
msgstr ""
"Cómo se ven los botones en la pantalla de ingreso. Es el mismo marcado y la "
"misma hoja de estilos que usa el sitio, así que la vista previa es lo que se"
" va a ver."

#: includes/admin-social.php:191
msgid "Finish"
msgstr "Acabado"

#: includes/admin-social.php:198
msgid ""
"Google and Microsoft always stay white with their own logo: their brand "
"guidelines ask for it, and a four-colour logo on a coloured background does "
"not read."
msgstr ""
"Google y Microsoft quedan siempre en blanco con su propio logo: lo piden sus"
" guías de marca, y un logo de cuatro colores sobre un fondo de color no se "
"lee."

#: includes/admin-social.php:202
msgid "Shape"
msgstr "Forma"

#: includes/admin-social.php:212
msgid "What it shows"
msgstr "Qué muestra"

#: includes/admin-social.php:219
msgid "With logo only, the name is still there for screen readers."
msgstr ""
"Con sólo el logo, el nombre sigue estando para los lectores de pantalla."

#: includes/admin-social.php:223
msgid "Layout"
msgstr "Disposición"

#: includes/admin-social.php:233 includes/fields.php:22
msgid "Text"
msgstr "Texto"

#. translators: %s: name of the social network
#: includes/admin-social.php:238 includes/sso-buttons.php:80
#, php-format
msgid "Continue with %s"
msgstr "Continuar con %s"

#. translators: %s: the %s placeholder, literal
#: includes/admin-social.php:243
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Where %s goes, the name of the network goes. Leave it empty to use the "
"default, which is already translated."
msgstr ""
"Donde va %s va el nombre de la red. Dejalo vacío para usar el texto por "
"defecto, que ya viene traducido."

#: includes/admin-social.php:256
msgid "Preview"
msgstr "Vista previa"

#: includes/admin-social.php:259
msgid "On white"
msgstr "Sobre blanco"

#: includes/admin-social.php:260
msgid "On dark"
msgstr "Sobre oscuro"

#: includes/admin-social.php:266
msgid "These buttons do nothing: they are here to be looked at."
msgstr "Estos botones no hacen nada: están para mirarlos."

#: includes/admin-social.php:274
msgid ""
"These apply to every provider. They decide what happens when someone comes "
"back from a social network."
msgstr ""
"Valen para todas las redes. Deciden qué pasa cuando alguien vuelve de una "
"red social."

#: includes/admin-social.php:280
msgid "Recognise people by email"
msgstr "Reconocer a la persona por el correo"

#: includes/admin-social.php:284
msgid "If the email already exists, link the network to that account"
msgstr "Si el correo ya existe, vincular la red a esa cuenta"

#: includes/admin-social.php:287
msgid ""
"This is what makes signing in with Google today and with GitHub tomorrow "
"land on the same account instead of creating two. Each network the person "
"uses gets added to their account, and any of them works from then on."
msgstr ""
"Esto es lo que hace que entrar con Google hoy y con GitHub mañana caiga en "
"la misma cuenta y no cree dos. Cada red que la persona usa se le suma a su "
"cuenta, y de ahí en más cualquiera le sirve."

#: includes/admin-social.php:290
msgid ""
"Turned off, someone whose email is already registered simply cannot get in "
"with a social network. Only turn it off if you do not trust the provider to "
"verify its own users’ email addresses."
msgstr ""
"Desactivada, alguien cuyo correo ya está registrado directamente no puede "
"entrar con una red social. Desactívala solo si no confías en que el "
"proveedor verifique el correo de su propia gente."

#: includes/admin-social.php:295
msgid "Create accounts"
msgstr "Crear cuentas"

#: includes/admin-social.php:299
msgid "If the email does not exist yet, create the account"
msgstr "Si el correo todavía no existe, crear la cuenta"

#: includes/admin-social.php:301
msgid ""
"Turned off, only people who already have an account can use the social "
"buttons."
msgstr ""
"Desactivada, solo quien ya tiene cuenta puede usar los botones de redes."

#: includes/admin-social.php:305
msgid "Verified email only"
msgstr "Sólo correo verificado"

#: includes/admin-social.php:309
msgid ""
"Refuse the sign-in when the provider does not say the email is verified"
msgstr ""
"Rechazar el ingreso cuando el proveedor no diga que el correo está "
"verificado"

#: includes/admin-social.php:311
msgid ""
"Stricter, and a few providers never send that flag: with this on, those stop"
" working."
msgstr ""
"Más estricto, y algunos proveedores nunca envían ese dato: con esto "
"activado, esos dejan de funcionar."

#: includes/admin-social.php:315
msgid "Roles that cannot use it"
msgstr "Roles que no pueden usarlo"

#: includes/admin-social.php:328
msgid ""
"People with one of these roles have to use the email link. It is the account"
" with the most power that is worth protecting: an administrator who signs in"
" with Google depends on that Google account never being taken over."
msgstr ""
"Quien tenga alguno de estos roles entra por el enlace de correo. La cuenta "
"con más poder es la que conviene proteger: un administrador que entra con "
"Google depende de que esa cuenta de Google nunca se la quede otro."

#: includes/admin-social.php:331
msgid "Nobody is locked out by this: the email link is always there."
msgstr "Esto no deja a nadie afuera: el enlace por correo siempre está."

#: includes/admin-social.php:340
msgid ""
"How an account ends up, and how one person ends up with several networks"
msgstr "Cómo queda una cuenta, y cómo una persona termina con varias redes"

#. translators: 1: name of the role accounts are created with, 2: name of the
#. screen where it is chosen
#: includes/admin-social.php:345
#, php-format
msgid ""
"There is nothing to choose here, and that is on purpose: a new account gets "
"the email address as its username, no password at all —not even one nobody "
"knows how to use— and the role %1$s, which is set once for the whole site on"
" the %2$s screen, because a role per provider would be a quiet way of "
"handing out privileges. The name comes from the provider and only fills in "
"what the person has not written themselves. Each linked network is stored on"
" the person, so anybody can add a second and a third from their profile and "
"unlink them again, and from then on any of them opens the same account."
msgstr ""
"Aquí no hay nada que elegir, y es a propósito: una cuenta nueva se crea con "
"el correo como nombre de usuario, sin contraseña ninguna —ni siquiera una "
"que nadie sepa usar— y con el rol %1$s, que se define una vez para todo el "
"sitio en la pantalla %2$s, porque un rol por proveedor sería una forma "
"silenciosa de repartir privilegios. El nombre lo trae el proveedor y solo "
"completa lo que la persona no ha escrito. Cada red vinculada se guarda en la"
" persona, así que cualquiera puede añadir una segunda y una tercera desde su"
" perfil y desvincularlas, y de ahí en adelante cualquiera de ellas abre la "
"misma cuenta."

